From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Agent <claude-agent@invalid>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 20:15:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] tests/color-management: Cover highlight mapping and scanout
 parity
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Extend the color-hdr conformance test. Expected curve values come from a
BT.2390 EETF (highlight compression only, no black level lift) and an
ST 2084 implementation written out in the test, in double precision;
the blending states are built the way the renderer view builds them,
from the output color state with a sample target (0.0005 to
600 cd/m²) attached:

 - /color-hdr/mapping/predicate: PQ, HLG (1000 cd/m² nominal peak),
   mastering 4000 and MaxCLL 1000 sources exceed the target; SDR,
   content mastered at or below the target and MaxCLL 500 do not; no
   mapping without a target, toward the output state, or from the
   blending state to the output or to itself; with reference white at
   700 cd/m², above the target, SDR white exceeds it (reference-white
   scaling); the target is part of color state equality; the output
   state with the target attached directly, which has no display
   reference, is not a display target.
 - /color-hdr/mapping/extended-range-peak: linear sRGB with reference
   white at 80 cd/m² (scRGB-style) has no known peak without
   declarations and is not mapped; a 1000 cd/m² mastering maximum or a
   4000 or 400 cd/m² MaxCLL gives that peak and is mapped; a bounded
   encoding (gamma 2.2 sRGB) keeps its maximum as a bound whatever its
   MaxCLL.
 - /color-hdr/mapping/cache-parity: two PQ sources mastered at
   590 cd/m², with reference white 203 and 196 cd/m², are equal by
   clutter_color_state_equals() but only the second is mapped; the
   transform cache gives them different transforms, and PQ white
   reaches the target through the mapped one only.
 - /color-hdr/mapping/identity: when not mapped, the conversion through
   the transform cache is bit-identical to the one toward the blending
   state without a target; without a target PQ white keeps its
   10000 cd/m²; content mastered at the target in the output's encoding
   needs no conversion to the output and no mapping.
 - /color-hdr/mapping/bt2390-reference: neutral PQ at 0.01 to
   10000 cd/m² matches the independent curve, through both the
   forced-linear and the gamma 2.2 blending state, with the output's
   reference white at 203, 102 and 264 cd/m² (reference luminance
   factors 1, 0.5 and 1.3, rounded as the colour device does); neutral
   HLG signals are decoded for 1000 cd/m² and then follow the curve; with
   a target black (0.05 cd/m²) above the source's, dark PQ content from
   0.001 cd/m², below the source minimum, to 10 cd/m² is left as the
   unmapped conversion gives it. Mapped values are compared relatively,
   so dark values are checked too.
 - /color-hdr/mapping/monotonic: a 1025-step PQ ramp is monotonic,
   never exceeds the target peak or the unmapped value, and reaches the
   target peak at the source peak.
 - /color-hdr/mapping/keeps-hue: channel ratios are kept, a negative
   component stays negative and a sample without a positive component
   is unchanged.
 - /color-hdr/mapping/shader-matches-cpu: the GLSL EETF matches the CPU
   one, with exact floating point input.

And a compositor regression, /wayland/mapping/blending-target, run in
its own invocation since it gives the fixture output a declared
600 cd/m² peak: the view's output color state stays the device's
encoding-only state while its blending state carries the target in the
display's units; for sources in the output's encoding, direct scanout
is refused by meta_compositor_view_native_color_state_prevents_scanout()
exactly when clutter_color_transform_requires_highlight_mapping() holds
and exactly when the renderer's conversion of bright content differs
from the unmapped one; a different encoding still prevents scanout
without mapping. With reference luminance factors 0.5 and 1.3, the
output's reference white is 102 and 264 cd/m², whole as published; a
source with that published reference white mastered at the declared
peak is neither mapped nor refused scanout, undeclared PQ is mapped,
and PQ mastered at the declared peak with the default reference white
is mapped only when the factor raises the output's reference white.
Once the peak is no longer declared, the blending state has no target,
nothing is mapped and scanout is allowed.

The hardware cursor plane decision is not covered: the test backends'
virtual monitors have no KMS CRTC, so the native cursor renderer never
reaches it without new test infrastructure.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DLZiLBYev72J1s4D37L7Bi
---
 src/tests/clutter/conform/color-hdr.c     | 705 +++++++++++++++++++++-
 src/tests/meson.build                     |   4 +-
 src/tests/wayland-color-management-test.c | 252 ++++++++
 3 files changed, 958 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/tests/clutter/conform/color-hdr.c b/src/tests/clutter/conform/color-hdr.c
index 190024438..b0d3c1a12 100644
--- a/src/tests/clutter/conform/color-hdr.c
+++ b/src/tests/clutter/conform/color-hdr.c
@@ -1,13 +1,16 @@
 /*
- * Regressions for HDR color operations: HLG decoding and encoding.
+ * Regressions for HDR color operations: HLG decoding and encoding, and the
+ * BT.2390 highlight mapping toward a display's target luminance.
  *
  * Expected values are computed here, in double precision, directly from the
- * formulas of Rec. ITU-R BT.2100-2, not by calling the code under test.
+ * formulas of Rec. ITU-R BT.2100-2 and Report ITU-R BT.2390, not by calling
+ * the code under test.
  */
 
 #include <math.h>
 
 #include "clutter-mutter.h"
+#include "clutter/clutter/clutter-color-state-params-private.h"
 #include "clutter/clutter/clutter-color-transform-private.h"
 #include "clutter/clutter/clutter-color-utils-private.h"
 #include "clutter/clutter/clutter-color-pipeline.h"
@@ -490,6 +493,696 @@ hlg_shader_matches_cpu (void)
     }
 }
 
+/* A sample display target, below the PQ encoding's 10000 cd/m². */
+#define TARGET_MIN_LUM 0.0005f
+#define TARGET_MAX_LUM 600.0f
+
+/* SMPTE ST 2084, written out separately from the code under test. */
+static double
+reference_pq_signal (double luminance)
+{
+  double m1 = 2610.0 / 16384.0;
+  double m2 = 2523.0 / 4096.0 * 128.0;
+  double c1 = 3424.0 / 4096.0;
+  double c2 = 2413.0 / 4096.0 * 32.0;
+  double c3 = 2392.0 / 4096.0 * 32.0;
+  double p = pow (MAX (luminance, 0.0) / 10000.0, m1);
+
+  return pow ((c1 + c2 * p) / (1.0 + c3 * p), m2);
+}
+
+static double
+reference_pq_luminance (double signal)
+{
+  double m1 = 2610.0 / 16384.0;
+  double m2 = 2523.0 / 4096.0 * 128.0;
+  double c1 = 3424.0 / 4096.0;
+  double c2 = 2413.0 / 4096.0 * 32.0;
+  double c3 = 2392.0 / 4096.0 * 32.0;
+  double p = pow (MAX (signal, 0.0), 1.0 / m2);
+
+  return 10000.0 * pow (MAX (p - c1, 0.0) / (c2 - c3 * p), 1.0 / m1);
+}
+
+/*
+ * Report ITU-R BT.2390 EETF on absolute luminance, highlight compression
+ * only: source range [source_min, source_max] normalized in the PQ domain,
+ * the Hermite knee at KS = 1.5 maxLum - 0.5 toward target_max, and no black
+ * level lift (b = 0), so the target minimum plays no part.
+ */
+static double
+reference_bt2390 (double luminance,
+                  double source_min,
+                  double source_max,
+                  double target_max)
+{
+  double source_min_pq = reference_pq_signal (source_min);
+  double source_range = reference_pq_signal (source_max) - source_min_pq;
+  double max_lum = (reference_pq_signal (target_max) - source_min_pq) / source_range;
+  double ks = 1.5 * max_lum - 0.5;
+  double e1, e2;
+
+  /* Above the source peak, the curve stays at the target peak. */
+  e1 = (reference_pq_signal (luminance) - source_min_pq) / source_range;
+  e1 = MIN (e1, 1.0);
+
+  if (e1 < ks)
+    {
+      e2 = e1;
+    }
+  else
+    {
+      double t = (e1 - ks) / (1.0 - ks);
+
+      e2 = (2.0 * pow (t, 3) - 3.0 * pow (t, 2) + 1.0) * ks +
+           (pow (t, 3) - 2.0 * pow (t, 2) + t) * (1.0 - ks) +
+           (-2.0 * pow (t, 3) + 3.0 * pow (t, 2)) * max_lum;
+    }
+
+  return reference_pq_luminance (e2 * source_range + source_min_pq);
+}
+
+static ClutterColorState *
+create_pq_output (float ref_lum)
+{
+  return clutter_color_state_params_new_full (clutter_test_get_context (),
+                                              CLUTTER_COLORSPACE_BT2020,
+                                              CLUTTER_TRANSFER_FUNCTION_PQ,
+                                              NULL, -1.0f,
+                                              0.005f, 10000.0f, ref_lum,
+                                              -1.0f);
+}
+
+/* Builds an output's blending state the way the renderer view does, from
+ * the output color state with the display's target luminance attached. */
+static ClutterColorState *
+create_targeted_blending_full (ClutterColorState *output,
+                               float              target_min,
+                               float              target_max,
+                               gboolean           force_linear)
+{
+  ClutterColorTargetVolume target_volume = {
+    .has_luminance = TRUE,
+    .min_lum = target_min,
+    .max_lum = target_max,
+  };
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) targeted = NULL;
+
+  targeted =
+    clutter_color_state_params_new_with_target_volume (CLUTTER_COLOR_STATE_PARAMS (output),
+                                                       &target_volume);
+
+  return clutter_color_state_get_blending (targeted, force_linear);
+}
+
+static ClutterColorState *
+create_targeted_blending (ClutterColorState *output,
+                          float              target_max,
+                          gboolean           force_linear)
+{
+  return create_targeted_blending_full (output, TARGET_MIN_LUM, target_max,
+                                        force_linear);
+}
+
+static ClutterColorState *
+create_with_target_volume (ClutterColorState *color_state,
+                           float              mastering_max,
+                           float              max_cll)
+{
+  ClutterColorTargetVolume target_volume = {
+    .has_luminance = mastering_max > 0.0f,
+    .min_lum = 0.0001f,
+    .max_lum = mastering_max,
+    .max_cll = max_cll,
+  };
+
+  return clutter_color_state_params_new_with_target_volume (CLUTTER_COLOR_STATE_PARAMS (color_state),
+                                                            &target_volume);
+}
+
+static void
+mapping_predicate (void)
+{
+  ClutterContext *context = clutter_test_get_context ();
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) output = create_pq_output (203.0f);
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) blending = NULL;
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) linear_blending = NULL;
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) untargeted_blending = NULL;
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) pq = NULL;
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) hlg = NULL;
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) srgb = NULL;
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) mastered_above = NULL;
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) mastered_at = NULL;
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) mastered_below = NULL;
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) cll_above = NULL;
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) cll_below = NULL;
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) bright_output = NULL;
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) bright_blending = NULL;
+
+  blending = create_targeted_blending (output, TARGET_MAX_LUM, FALSE);
+  linear_blending = create_targeted_blending (output, TARGET_MAX_LUM, TRUE);
+  untargeted_blending = clutter_color_state_get_blending (output, FALSE);
+
+  pq = clutter_color_state_params_new (context, CLUTTER_COLORSPACE_BT2020,
+                                       CLUTTER_TRANSFER_FUNCTION_PQ);
+  hlg = clutter_color_state_params_new (context, CLUTTER_COLORSPACE_BT2020,
+                                        CLUTTER_TRANSFER_FUNCTION_HLG);
+  srgb = clutter_color_state_params_new (context, CLUTTER_COLORSPACE_SRGB,
+                                         CLUTTER_TRANSFER_FUNCTION_GAMMA22);
+  mastered_above = create_with_target_volume (pq, 4000.0f, 0.0f);
+  mastered_at = create_with_target_volume (pq, TARGET_MAX_LUM, 0.0f);
+  mastered_below = create_with_target_volume (pq, 400.0f, 0.0f);
+  cll_above = create_with_target_volume (pq, 0.0f, 1000.0f);
+  cll_below = create_with_target_volume (pq, 4000.0f, 500.0f);
+
+  /* The effective source peak exceeds the target. */
+  g_assert_true (clutter_color_transform_requires_highlight_mapping (pq, blending));
+  g_assert_true (clutter_color_transform_requires_highlight_mapping (pq, linear_blending));
+  g_assert_true (clutter_color_transform_requires_highlight_mapping (hlg, blending));
+  g_assert_true (clutter_color_transform_requires_highlight_mapping (mastered_above, blending));
+  g_assert_true (clutter_color_transform_requires_highlight_mapping (cll_above, blending));
+
+  /* At or below the target: no mapping, never expansion. SDR reference
+   * white is 203 cd/m² on this output. */
+  g_assert_false (clutter_color_transform_requires_highlight_mapping (srgb, blending));
+  g_assert_false (clutter_color_transform_requires_highlight_mapping (mastered_at, blending));
+  g_assert_false (clutter_color_transform_requires_highlight_mapping (mastered_below, blending));
+  g_assert_false (clutter_color_transform_requires_highlight_mapping (cll_below, blending));
+
+  /* No declared target: no mapping. */
+  g_assert_false (clutter_color_transform_requires_highlight_mapping (pq, untargeted_blending));
+  g_assert_false (clutter_color_transform_requires_highlight_mapping (pq, output));
+
+  /* Blended content is already mapped: not again to the output. */
+  g_assert_false (clutter_color_transform_requires_highlight_mapping (blending, output));
+  g_assert_false (clutter_color_transform_requires_highlight_mapping (linear_blending, output));
+  g_assert_false (clutter_color_transform_requires_highlight_mapping (blending, blending));
+
+  /* The comparison follows reference-white scaling: with reference white
+   * at 700 cd/m², above the target, SDR white itself exceeds it. */
+  bright_output = create_pq_output (700.0f);
+  bright_blending = create_targeted_blending (bright_output, TARGET_MAX_LUM, FALSE);
+  g_assert_true (clutter_color_transform_requires_highlight_mapping (srgb, bright_blending));
+  g_assert_false (clutter_color_transform_requires_highlight_mapping (srgb, blending));
+
+  /* The target is part of the color state identity. */
+  g_assert_false (clutter_color_state_equals (blending, untargeted_blending));
+
+  /* Only a blending state derived for a display target is one: the output
+   * color state with a target attached, from which it is derived, is not. */
+  {
+    ClutterColorTargetVolume target_volume = {
+      .has_luminance = TRUE,
+      .min_lum = TARGET_MIN_LUM,
+      .max_lum = TARGET_MAX_LUM,
+    };
+    g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) targeted_output = NULL;
+
+    targeted_output =
+      clutter_color_state_params_new_with_target_volume (CLUTTER_COLOR_STATE_PARAMS (output),
+                                                         &target_volume);
+    g_assert_false (clutter_color_transform_requires_highlight_mapping (pq, targeted_output));
+    g_assert_false (clutter_color_transform_requires_highlight_mapping (mastered_above,
+                                                                        targeted_output));
+  }
+}
+
+/*
+ * An extended-range encoding (linear, as ext_linear or scRGB content) does
+ * not bound its peak by its nominal maximum: only MaxCLL or a mastering
+ * maximum does, and without either the peak is unknown and nothing is
+ * mapped. Bounded encodings keep the encoding maximum as a bound.
+ */
+static void
+mapping_extended_range_peak (void)
+{
+  ClutterContext *context = clutter_test_get_context ();
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) output = create_pq_output (203.0f);
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) blending = NULL;
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) linear = NULL;
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) linear_mastered = NULL;
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) linear_cll = NULL;
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) linear_dim = NULL;
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) srgb = NULL;
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) srgb_cll = NULL;
+  double min_headroom, peak_headroom;
+
+  blending = create_targeted_blending (output, TARGET_MAX_LUM, FALSE);
+  /* scRGB-style: linear sRGB with reference white at 80 cd/m², where values
+   * far above 1.0 carry HDR highlights. */
+  linear = clutter_color_state_params_new (context, CLUTTER_COLORSPACE_SRGB,
+                                           CLUTTER_TRANSFER_FUNCTION_LINEAR);
+  linear_mastered = create_with_target_volume (linear, 1000.0f, 0.0f);
+  linear_cll = create_with_target_volume (linear, 0.0f, 4000.0f);
+  linear_dim = create_with_target_volume (linear, 0.0f, 400.0f);
+  srgb = clutter_color_state_params_new (context, CLUTTER_COLORSPACE_SRGB,
+                                         CLUTTER_TRANSFER_FUNCTION_GAMMA22);
+  srgb_cll = create_with_target_volume (srgb, 0.0f, 4000.0f);
+
+  g_assert_false (clutter_color_state_params_get_peak_headroom (CLUTTER_COLOR_STATE_PARAMS (linear),
+                                                                &min_headroom,
+                                                                &peak_headroom));
+  g_assert_false (clutter_color_transform_requires_highlight_mapping (linear, blending));
+
+  /* Declared peaks: 1000 and 4000 cd/m² over 80 exceed 600 over 203. */
+  g_assert_true (clutter_color_state_params_get_peak_headroom (CLUTTER_COLOR_STATE_PARAMS (linear_mastered),
+                                                               &min_headroom,
+                                                               &peak_headroom));
+  g_assert_cmpfloat_with_epsilon (peak_headroom, 1000.0 / 80.0, 1e-9);
+  g_assert_true (clutter_color_transform_requires_highlight_mapping (linear_mastered, blending));
+  g_assert_true (clutter_color_transform_requires_highlight_mapping (linear_cll, blending));
+
+  /* 400 cd/m² over 80 is 5 times reference white, above 600 over 203. */
+  g_assert_true (clutter_color_state_params_get_peak_headroom (CLUTTER_COLOR_STATE_PARAMS (linear_dim),
+                                                               NULL,
+                                                               &peak_headroom));
+  g_assert_cmpfloat_with_epsilon (peak_headroom, 400.0 / 80.0, 1e-9);
+  g_assert_true (clutter_color_transform_requires_highlight_mapping (linear_dim, blending));
+
+  /* A bounded encoding keeps its maximum as a bound: SDR never exceeds
+   * reference white, whatever MaxCLL says. */
+  g_assert_true (clutter_color_state_params_get_peak_headroom (CLUTTER_COLOR_STATE_PARAMS (srgb_cll),
+                                                               NULL,
+                                                               &peak_headroom));
+  g_assert_cmpfloat_with_epsilon (peak_headroom, 1.0, 1e-9);
+  g_assert_false (clutter_color_transform_requires_highlight_mapping (srgb_cll, blending));
+}
+
+/*
+ * The transform cache must tell apart states that clutter_color_state_equals()
+ * deems equal (luminances within 10%) when they differ in whether they are
+ * mapped: one mapped and one unmapped surface must not share a pipeline.
+ */
+static void
+mapping_cache_parity (void)
+{
+  ClutterContext *context = clutter_test_get_context ();
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) output = create_pq_output (203.0f);
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) blending = NULL;
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) pq_203 = NULL;
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) pq_196 = NULL;
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) below = NULL;
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) above = NULL;
+  ClutterColorTransform *below_transform, *above_transform;
+  float below_white[4] = { 1.0f, 1.0f, 1.0f, 1.0f };
+  float above_white[4] = { 1.0f, 1.0f, 1.0f, 1.0f };
+
+  blending = create_targeted_blending (output, TARGET_MAX_LUM, FALSE);
+  pq_203 = clutter_color_state_params_new_full (context,
+                                                CLUTTER_COLORSPACE_BT2020,
+                                                CLUTTER_TRANSFER_FUNCTION_PQ,
+                                                NULL, -1.0f,
+                                                0.005f, 10000.0f, 203.0f,
+                                                -1.0f);
+  pq_196 = clutter_color_state_params_new_full (context,
+                                                CLUTTER_COLORSPACE_BT2020,
+                                                CLUTTER_TRANSFER_FUNCTION_PQ,
+                                                NULL, -1.0f,
+                                                0.005f, 10000.0f, 196.0f,
+                                                -1.0f);
+  /* Mastered at 590 cd/m²: below the 600 cd/m² target with reference white
+   * at 203, above it with reference white at 196. */
+  below = create_with_target_volume (pq_203, 590.0f, 0.0f);
+  above = create_with_target_volume (pq_196, 590.0f, 0.0f);
+
+  g_assert_true (clutter_color_state_equals (below, above));
+  g_assert_false (clutter_color_transform_requires_highlight_mapping (below, blending));
+  g_assert_true (clutter_color_transform_requires_highlight_mapping (above, blending));
+
+  below_transform = clutter_color_transform_from_color_states (context, below,
+                                                               blending, 0);
+  above_transform = clutter_color_transform_from_color_states (context, above,
+                                                               blending, 0);
+  g_assert_true (below_transform != above_transform);
+
+  /* PQ white, 10000 cd/m², is mapped to the target for one only. */
+  clutter_color_pipeline_do_transform (clutter_color_transform_get_pipeline (below_transform),
+                                       below_white, 1);
+  clutter_color_pipeline_do_transform (clutter_color_transform_get_pipeline (above_transform),
+                                       above_white, 1);
+  g_assert_cmpfloat_with_epsilon (above_white[0],
+                                  pow (TARGET_MAX_LUM / 203.0, 1.0 / 2.2),
+                                  1e-3);
+  g_assert_cmpfloat (below_white[0], >, above_white[0] * 2.0f);
+}
+
+static void
+assert_pipelines_equal (ClutterColorState *source,
+                        ClutterColorState *target,
+                        ClutterColorState *other_target)
+{
+  ClutterContext *context = clutter_test_get_context ();
+  ClutterColorTransform *transform, *other_transform;
+  int i;
+
+  /* Through the transform cache, as the renderer gets them. */
+  transform = clutter_color_transform_from_color_states (context, source,
+                                                         target, 0);
+  other_transform = clutter_color_transform_from_color_states (context, source,
+                                                               other_target, 0);
+
+  for (i = 0; i < G_N_ELEMENTS (hlg_signals); i++)
+    {
+      float a[4] = { hlg_signals[i][0], hlg_signals[i][1], hlg_signals[i][2], 1.0f };
+      float b[4] = { hlg_signals[i][0], hlg_signals[i][1], hlg_signals[i][2], 1.0f };
+
+      clutter_color_pipeline_do_transform (clutter_color_transform_get_pipeline (transform),
+                                           a, 1);
+      clutter_color_pipeline_do_transform (clutter_color_transform_get_pipeline (other_transform),
+                                           b, 1);
+      g_assert_cmpfloat (a[0], ==, b[0]);
+      g_assert_cmpfloat (a[1], ==, b[1]);
+      g_assert_cmpfloat (a[2], ==, b[2]);
+    }
+}
+
+static void
+mapping_identity (void)
+{
+  ClutterContext *context = clutter_test_get_context ();
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) output = create_pq_output (203.0f);
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) blending = NULL;
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) untargeted_blending = NULL;
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) pq = NULL;
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) srgb = NULL;
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) mastered_below = NULL;
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) mastered_at = NULL;
+  const float white[3] = { 1.0f, 1.0f, 1.0f };
+  float output_color[4];
+  double expected;
+
+  blending = create_targeted_blending (output, TARGET_MAX_LUM, FALSE);
+  untargeted_blending = clutter_color_state_get_blending (output, FALSE);
+  pq = clutter_color_state_params_new (context, CLUTTER_COLORSPACE_BT2020,
+                                       CLUTTER_TRANSFER_FUNCTION_PQ);
+  srgb = clutter_color_state_params_new (context, CLUTTER_COLORSPACE_SRGB,
+                                         CLUTTER_TRANSFER_FUNCTION_GAMMA22);
+  mastered_below = create_with_target_volume (pq, 400.0f, 0.0f);
+  mastered_at = create_with_target_volume (pq, TARGET_MAX_LUM, 0.0f);
+
+  /* At or below the target, the conversion is the one without a target. */
+  assert_pipelines_equal (srgb, blending, untargeted_blending);
+  assert_pipelines_equal (mastered_below, blending, untargeted_blending);
+  assert_pipelines_equal (mastered_at, blending, untargeted_blending);
+
+  /* Without a target, PQ white keeps its 10000 cd/m²: in the extended
+   * gamma 2.2 blending space reference white (203 cd/m²) is 1.0. */
+  transform_one (pq, untargeted_blending, white, output_color);
+  expected = pow (10000.0 / 203.0, 1.0 / 2.2);
+  g_assert_cmpfloat_with_epsilon (output_color[0], expected, 1e-3 * expected);
+
+  /* Content already mapped to the target, in the output's encoding, needs
+   * no conversion to the output at all. */
+  g_assert_false (clutter_color_pipeline_shader_needs_color_state (mastered_at, output, 0));
+  g_assert_false (clutter_color_transform_requires_highlight_mapping (mastered_at, blending));
+}
+
+static void
+assert_mapped_neutral (ClutterColorState *source,
+                       ClutterColorState *blending,
+                       float              signal,
+                       double             expected,
+                       const char        *name)
+{
+  const float input[3] = { signal, signal, signal };
+  float output_color[4];
+  int c;
+
+  transform_one (source, blending, input, output_color);
+  for (c = 0; c < 3; c++)
+    {
+      /* Relative, so that dark values are checked too. */
+      if (fabs (output_color[c] - expected) > 2e-3 * fabs (expected) + 1e-7)
+        {
+          g_error ("BT.2390 mapping (%s) of signal %.6f, channel %d: "
+                   "%.6f, expected %.6f",
+                   name, signal, c, output_color[c], expected);
+        }
+    }
+}
+
+/*
+ * Neutral PQ through the blending states of an output whose reference white
+ * is at @output_ref cd/m². Reference-white anchoring puts a source luminance
+ * L at L * output ref / source ref on the display.
+ */
+static void
+assert_pq_mapping_matches_reference (float output_ref)
+{
+  static const double luminances[] = {
+    0.01, 0.1, 1.0, 10.0, 100.0, 203.0, 400.0, 600.0, 1000.0, 4000.0, 10000.0,
+  };
+  ClutterContext *context = clutter_test_get_context ();
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) output = create_pq_output (output_ref);
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) blending = NULL;
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) linear_blending = NULL;
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) pq = NULL;
+  const ClutterLuminance *pq_lum, *linear_lum;
+  double anchoring;
+  int i;
+
+  blending = create_targeted_blending (output, TARGET_MAX_LUM, FALSE);
+  linear_blending = create_targeted_blending (output, TARGET_MAX_LUM, TRUE);
+  pq = clutter_color_state_params_new (context, CLUTTER_COLORSPACE_BT2020,
+                                       CLUTTER_TRANSFER_FUNCTION_PQ);
+  pq_lum = clutter_color_state_get_luminance (pq);
+  linear_lum = clutter_color_state_get_luminance (linear_blending);
+  anchoring = output_ref / (double) pq_lum->ref;
+
+  for (i = 0; i < G_N_ELEMENTS (luminances); i++)
+    {
+      float signal = (float) reference_pq_signal (luminances[i]);
+      /* PQ linear light is normalized to the state's maximum. */
+      double luminance =
+        reference_pq_luminance (signal) / 10000.0 * pq_lum->max * anchoring;
+      double mapped = reference_bt2390 (luminance,
+                                        pq_lum->min * anchoring,
+                                        pq_lum->max * anchoring,
+                                        TARGET_MAX_LUM);
+
+      /* Linear blending keeps the output's units. */
+      assert_mapped_neutral (pq, linear_blending, signal,
+                             mapped / linear_lum->max, "PQ, linear blending");
+
+      /* Gamma 2.2 blending has the output's reference white at 1.0. */
+      assert_mapped_neutral (pq, blending, signal,
+                             pow (mapped / output_ref, 1.0 / 2.2),
+                             "PQ, gamma 2.2 blending");
+    }
+}
+
+static void
+mapping_bt2390_reference (void)
+{
+  ClutterContext *context = clutter_test_get_context ();
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) output = create_pq_output (203.0f);
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) linear_blending = NULL;
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) pq = NULL;
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) hlg = NULL;
+  const ClutterLuminance *pq_lum, *linear_lum;
+  int i;
+
+  /* Reference luminance factors 1, 0.5 and 1.3: reference white at 203,
+   * round (101.5) and round (263.9) cd/m², as output states are built. */
+  assert_pq_mapping_matches_reference (203.0f);
+  assert_pq_mapping_matches_reference (102.0f);
+  assert_pq_mapping_matches_reference (264.0f);
+
+  linear_blending = create_targeted_blending (output, TARGET_MAX_LUM, TRUE);
+  pq = clutter_color_state_params_new (context, CLUTTER_COLORSPACE_BT2020,
+                                       CLUTTER_TRANSFER_FUNCTION_PQ);
+  hlg = clutter_color_state_params_new (context, CLUTTER_COLORSPACE_BT2020,
+                                        CLUTTER_TRANSFER_FUNCTION_HLG);
+  pq_lum = clutter_color_state_get_luminance (pq);
+  linear_lum = clutter_color_state_get_luminance (linear_blending);
+
+  /* HLG is decoded for its 1000 cd/m² nominal peak, then mapped. */
+  for (i = 0; i < G_N_ELEMENTS (hlg_signals); i++)
+    {
+      double display[3], mapped;
+
+      if (hlg_signals[i][0] != hlg_signals[i][1] ||
+          hlg_signals[i][0] != hlg_signals[i][2])
+        continue;
+
+      reference_hlg_eotf (hlg_signals[i], &hlg_cases[0], display);
+      mapped = reference_bt2390 (display[0] * 1000.0, 0.005, 1000.0,
+                                 TARGET_MAX_LUM);
+      assert_mapped_neutral (hlg, linear_blending, hlg_signals[i][0],
+                             mapped / linear_lum->max, "HLG, linear blending");
+    }
+
+  /* A target black above the source's is not used to raise black: below
+   * the knee, content is unchanged. */
+  {
+    static const double dark_luminances[] = { 0.001, 0.01, 0.1, 1.0, 10.0 };
+    g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) raised_black = NULL;
+    g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) untargeted = NULL;
+
+    raised_black = create_targeted_blending_full (output, 0.05f, TARGET_MAX_LUM,
+                                                  TRUE);
+    untargeted = clutter_color_state_get_blending (output, TRUE);
+    for (i = 0; i < G_N_ELEMENTS (dark_luminances); i++)
+      {
+        float signal = (float) reference_pq_signal (dark_luminances[i]);
+        double luminance = reference_pq_luminance (signal) / 10000.0 * pq_lum->max;
+        double mapped = reference_bt2390 (luminance,
+                                          pq_lum->min, pq_lum->max,
+                                          TARGET_MAX_LUM);
+
+        const float input[3] = { signal, signal, signal };
+        float with_target[4], without_target[4];
+
+        g_assert_cmpfloat_with_epsilon (mapped, luminance, 1e-9 * luminance);
+        assert_mapped_neutral (pq, raised_black, signal,
+                               mapped / linear_lum->max,
+                               "PQ, target black above source black");
+
+        /* Below the knee, the sample is left as the unmapped conversion
+         * gives it. */
+        transform_one (pq, raised_black, input, with_target);
+        transform_one (pq, untargeted, input, without_target);
+        g_assert_cmpfloat_with_epsilon (with_target[0], without_target[0],
+                                        1e-5 * without_target[0]);
+      }
+  }
+}
+
+static void
+mapping_monotonic (void)
+{
+  ClutterContext *context = clutter_test_get_context ();
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) output = create_pq_output (203.0f);
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) linear_blending = NULL;
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) untargeted = NULL;
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) pq = NULL;
+  const ClutterLuminance *lum;
+  float previous = 0.0f;
+  int i;
+
+  linear_blending = create_targeted_blending (output, TARGET_MAX_LUM, TRUE);
+  untargeted = clutter_color_state_get_blending (output, TRUE);
+  pq = clutter_color_state_params_new (context, CLUTTER_COLORSPACE_BT2020,
+                                       CLUTTER_TRANSFER_FUNCTION_PQ);
+  lum = clutter_color_state_get_luminance (linear_blending);
+
+  for (i = 0; i <= 1024; i++)
+    {
+      float signal = (float) i / 1024.0f;
+      const float input[3] = { signal, signal, signal };
+      float mapped[4], unmapped[4];
+
+      transform_one (pq, linear_blending, input, mapped);
+      transform_one (pq, untargeted, input, unmapped);
+
+      /* Monotonic, up to single precision rounding where the curve flattens
+       * toward the target peak. */
+      g_assert_cmpfloat (mapped[0], >=, previous - 2e-5f * previous);
+      /* Never above the target peak, never above the unmapped value. */
+      g_assert_cmpfloat (mapped[0] * lum->max, <=, TARGET_MAX_LUM * 1.0001f);
+      g_assert_cmpfloat (mapped[0], <=, unmapped[0] * 1.0001f + 1e-9f);
+      previous = mapped[0];
+    }
+
+  /* The source peak reaches the target peak. */
+  g_assert_cmpfloat_with_epsilon (previous * lum->max, TARGET_MAX_LUM,
+                                  1e-3f * TARGET_MAX_LUM);
+}
+
+static void
+mapping_keeps_hue (void)
+{
+  static const float colors[][3] = {
+    { 0.5f, 0.25f, 0.1f },
+    { 0.9f, 0.05f, 0.3f },
+    { 0.02f, 0.6f, 0.6f },
+    { 0.04f, 0.01f, 0.02f },
+    /* A negative component stays negative. */
+    { 0.3f, -0.01f, 0.2f },
+    /* Without a positive component, the sample is unchanged. */
+    { -0.1f, -0.2f, -0.05f },
+  };
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) output = create_pq_output (203.0f);
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) linear_blending = NULL;
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) untargeted = NULL;
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) linear = NULL;
+  int i, c;
+
+  linear_blending = create_targeted_blending (output, TARGET_MAX_LUM, TRUE);
+  untargeted = clutter_color_state_get_blending (output, TRUE);
+  /* Linear BT.2020 with PQ's range, so samples can be given directly. An
+   * extended-range encoding does not bound its peak: declare it. */
+  {
+    g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) undeclared = NULL;
+
+    undeclared = clutter_color_state_params_new_full (clutter_test_get_context (),
+                                                      CLUTTER_COLORSPACE_BT2020,
+                                                      CLUTTER_TRANSFER_FUNCTION_LINEAR,
+                                                      NULL, -1.0f,
+                                                      0.005f, 10000.0f, 203.0f,
+                                                      -1.0f);
+    linear = create_with_target_volume (undeclared, 10000.0f, 0.0f);
+  }
+  g_assert_true (clutter_color_transform_requires_highlight_mapping (linear,
+                                                                     linear_blending));
+
+  for (i = 0; i < G_N_ELEMENTS (colors); i++)
+    {
+      float mapped[4], unmapped[4];
+      double ratio = 0.0;
+
+      transform_one (linear, linear_blending, colors[i], mapped);
+      transform_one (linear, untargeted, colors[i], unmapped);
+
+      for (c = 0; c < 3; c++)
+        {
+          if (unmapped[c] == 0.0f)
+            {
+              g_assert_cmpfloat (mapped[c], ==, 0.0f);
+              continue;
+            }
+
+          if (ratio == 0.0)
+            ratio = mapped[c] / unmapped[c];
+          else
+            g_assert_cmpfloat_with_epsilon (mapped[c] / unmapped[c], ratio,
+                                            1e-4 * ratio);
+
+          g_assert_true ((mapped[c] < 0.0f) == (unmapped[c] < 0.0f));
+        }
+
+      if (MAX (colors[i][0], MAX (colors[i][1], colors[i][2])) <= 0.0f)
+        g_assert_cmpfloat_with_epsilon (ratio, 1.0, 1e-5);
+      else
+        g_assert_cmpfloat (ratio, <, 1.0);
+    }
+}
+
+static void
+mapping_shader_matches_cpu (void)
+{
+  ClutterContext *context = clutter_test_get_context ();
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) output = create_pq_output (203.0f);
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) blending = NULL;
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) linear_blending = NULL;
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) pq = NULL;
+  g_autoptr (ClutterColorState) hlg = NULL;
+
+  blending = create_targeted_blending (output, TARGET_MAX_LUM, FALSE);
+  linear_blending = create_targeted_blending (output, TARGET_MAX_LUM, TRUE);
+  pq = clutter_color_state_params_new (context, CLUTTER_COLORSPACE_BT2020,
+                                       CLUTTER_TRANSFER_FUNCTION_PQ);
+  hlg = clutter_color_state_params_new (context, CLUTTER_COLORSPACE_BT2020,
+                                        CLUTTER_TRANSFER_FUNCTION_HLG);
+
+  assert_shader_matches_cpu (pq, blending, hlg_signals,
+                             G_N_ELEMENTS (hlg_signals), 2e-3f);
+  assert_shader_matches_cpu (pq, linear_blending, hlg_signals,
+                             G_N_ELEMENTS (hlg_signals), 1e-4f);
+  assert_shader_matches_cpu (hlg, blending, hlg_signals,
+                             G_N_ELEMENTS (hlg_signals), 2e-3f);
+}
